{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0033", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Footnote 2", "locator": "fn2", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "\"Autonomy\" captures the potential misuse of AI models with significant capacity for agency and flexible action/tool use over long time horizons and across multiple domains.", "paraphrase": "This footnote defines Autonomy as misuse potential from agency and flexible action/tool use over long horizons and domains.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0034", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Footnote 3", "locator": "fn3", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Effective compute is a measure of the performance of a foundation model that uses scaling laws to integrate model size, dataset size, algorithmic progress, and compute into a single metric.", "paraphrase": "This footnote defines effective compute as a scaling-law-based single metric combining model size, dataset size, algorithmic progress, and compute.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0035", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Footnote 3", "locator": "fn3", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "While there is no direct relationship between effective compute and model size, a rough estimate suggests that a 6x increase in effective compute would correspond to approximately 2-2.5x increase in model size.", "paraphrase": "The footnote notes that a 6x effective compute increase roughly corresponds to a 2-2.5x model size increase, though no direct relationship exists.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "6x effective compute ≈ 2-2.5x model size", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0036", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Footnote 4", "locator": "fn4", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "More specifically, the early warning evaluations will be a set of model evaluations that we are confident will be passed before the model is 6x in effective compute or 3 months of fine-tuning away from the CCL.", "paraphrase": "This footnote clarifies early warning evaluations are expected to be passed before a model is within 6x effective compute or 3 months of fine-tuning of a CCL.", "modal_register": "mandatory", "stated_bar": "6x effective compute; 3 months of fine-tuning", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0037", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Figure 1 caption", "locator": "Figure 1", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Figure 1: the relationship between different components of the Framework.", "paraphrase": "Caption describing Figure 1's depiction of framework component relationships.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0038", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Mitigations", "locator": "Mitigations / para 1", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "The Frontier Safety Framework proposes two kinds of mitigations to address models with critical capabilities: security mitigations to prevent the exfiltration of model weights, and deployment mitigations to manage access to/prevent the expression of critical capabilities in deployments.", "paraphrase": "Two mitigation types are proposed: security mitigations against weight exfiltration and deployment mitigations to manage/prevent expression of critical capabilities.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0028", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0039", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Mitigations", "locator": "Mitigations / para 1", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "For each category of mitigation, we have developed several levels of mitigations, allowing us to calibrate the robustness of measures to the risks posed.", "paraphrase": "Multiple mitigation levels were developed per category to calibrate robustness to risk posed.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0040", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations", "locator": "Security Mitigations / para 1", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "The table below describes levels of security mitigations that may be applied to model weights to prevent their exfiltration.", "paraphrase": "The following table lists security mitigation levels applicable to model weights to prevent exfiltration.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0041", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations", "locator": "Security Mitigations / para 1", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "This is an important measure because the release of model weights may enable the removal of any safeguards trained into or deployed with the model, and hence access (including by bad actors) to any critical capabilities.", "paraphrase": "Preventing weight release is important because it could allow removal of safeguards and unauthorized access to critical capabilities.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0042", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations Table", "locator": "Security Table / Level 0 / Level and capabilities", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row: 0: Status quo. Column: Level and capabilities.", "excerpt": "0: Status quo", "paraphrase": "Security Level 0 is labeled Status quo.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0043", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations Table", "locator": "Security Table / Level 0 / Measures", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row: 0: Status quo. Column: Measures.", "excerpt": "Industry standard development and enterprise controls. E.g., multi-factor authentication, basic access control mechanisms, secure software development standards, red-team tests.", "paraphrase": "Level 0 measures consist of standard industry development and enterprise security controls.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0044", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations Table", "locator": "Security Table / Level 1 / Level and capabilities", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row: 1: Controlled access. Column: Level and capabilities.", "excerpt": "1: Controlled access. Access Control List hygiene. Non-forgeable lineage of models. Approximately RAND L3.", "paraphrase": "Level 1 (Controlled access) involves ACL hygiene and non-forgeable model lineage, approximately RAND L3.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "RAND L3", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0045", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations Table", "locator": "Security Table / Level 1 / Measures", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row: 1: Controlled access. Column: Measures.", "excerpt": "Limited access to raw representations of the most valuable models, including isolation of development models from production models. Specific measures include model and checkpoint storage lockdown, SLSA Build L3 for model provenance, and hardening of ML platforms and tools.", "paraphrase": "Level 1 measures limit access to valuable model representations and include storage lockdown, SLSA Build L3 provenance, and ML platform hardening.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "SLSA Build L3", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0046", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations Table", "locator": "Security Table / Level 2 / Level and capabilities", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row: 2: Lockdown of unilateral access. Column: Level and capabilities.", "excerpt": "2: Lockdown of unilateral access. Significant restrictions of unilateral access of model weights. Approximately RAND L3-L4.", "paraphrase": "Level 2 (Lockdown) significantly restricts unilateral access to weights, approximately RAND L3-L4.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "RAND L3-L4", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0047", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations Table", "locator": "Security Table / Level 2 / Measures", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row: 2: Lockdown of unilateral access. Column: Measures.", "excerpt": "Changes to ML platforms and tools to disallow unilateral access to raw model representations outside the core research team, with exceptions granted on the basis of business need.", "paraphrase": "Level 2 measures block unilateral raw model access outside the core team, with exceptions for business need.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0048", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Footnote 5", "locator": "fn5", "unit_type": "footnote", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "See https://www.rand.org/pubs/working_papers/WRA2849-1.html.", "paraphrase": "This footnote references a RAND working paper.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0049", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations Table", "locator": "Security Table / Level 3 / Level and capabilities", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row: 3: High-trust developer environments. Column: Level and capabilities.", "excerpt": "3: High-trust developer environments. For developers with unilateral access to raw models, protection against exfiltration and account compromise. Approximately RAND L4.", "paraphrase": "Level 3 provides protection against exfiltration and account compromise for developers with unilateral raw model access, approximately RAND L4.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "RAND L4", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0050", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations Table", "locator": "Security Table / Level 3 / Measures", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row: 3: High-trust developer environments. Column: Measures.", "excerpt": "Models can be accessed only through high-trust developer environments (HTDE), hardened, tamper-resistant workstations with enhanced logging.", "paraphrase": "Level 3 measures restrict model access to hardened, tamper-resistant, enhanced-logging workstations.", "modal_register": "mandatory", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0051", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations Table", "locator": "Security Table / Level 4 / Level and capabilities", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row: 4: Advanced protection. Column: Level and capabilities.", "excerpt": "4: Advanced protection. Model weights are generally not accessible to humans, even non-unilaterally. Hardened software platforms and confidential-compute hardware make it difficult even for well-funded adversaries to find and exploit vulnerabilities. Approximately RAND L5.", "paraphrase": "Level 4 makes weights generally inaccessible to humans, using hardened software and confidential-compute hardware, approximately RAND L5.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "RAND L5", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0052", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Security Mitigations Table", "locator": "Security Table / Level 4 / Measures", "unit_type": "table_cell", "context_stem": "Row: 4: Advanced protection. Column: Measures.", "excerpt": "Minimal trusted computing base (TCB). TPUs with confidential compute capabilities. Dedicated hardware pods for training and serving high-value models.", "paraphrase": "Level 4 measures include a minimal TCB, confidential-compute TPUs, and dedicated hardware pods for high-value models.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0053", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Deployment Mitigations", "locator": "Deployment Mitigations / para 1", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "This table below describes levels of deployment mitigations that may be applied to models and their descendants to manage access to and limit the expression of critical capabilities in deployment.", "paraphrase": "The following table describes deployment mitigation levels to manage/limit critical capability expression in deployed models and their descendants.", "modal_register": "conditional", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0054", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Deployment Mitigations", "locator": "Deployment Mitigations / para 1", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Critical capabilities may have closely associated positive capabilities, misuse of critical capabilities may be more or less difficult to distinguish from beneficial uses, and the overall risks of misuse may differ by deployment context.", "paraphrase": "Critical capabilities can be closely tied to beneficial uses, complicating misuse detection, and risk varies with deployment context.", "modal_register": "none", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
{"unit_id": "GDM-FSF-v1-0-0055", "source_version": "target", "lab_name": "Google DeepMind", "framework_name": "Frontier Safety Framework", "framework_version": "Version 1.0", "framework_year": 2024, "section_heading": "Deployment Mitigations", "locator": "Deployment Mitigations / para 1", "unit_type": "paragraph", "context_stem": "NONE", "excerpt": "Because of this, the mitigation options listed below are illustrative and will need to be tailored to different use cases and risks.", "paraphrase": "The listed mitigation options are illustrative examples that must be adapted to specific use cases and risks.", "modal_register": "mandatory", "stated_bar": "NONE", "duplicate_of": "NONE", "removal_candidate": false, "prior_locator": "NONE", "prior_counterpart_excerpt": "NONE", "prior_modal_register": "NONE", "prior_stated_bar": "NONE", "alignment_note": "NONE"}
